      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(ui): reset routed sessions to main on restore",
        "body": "Closes #61661\nRelated #61661\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where Control UI reloads could reopen a stale historical routed session from older browser-local routed keys instead of returning users to the real `main` session. The fix also needs to preserve valid scoped `sessionsByGateway` routed selections for the active gateway so supported routed restores keep working.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis change confines the behavior fix to Control UI restore sanitization. Historical top-level routed keys are normalized back to `main`, while valid per-gateway routed selections are preserved explicitly so compatible routed restores remain sticky. Live gateway routing, backend session semantics, and broader routed-session persistence policy changes remain out of scope.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers who reload the Control UI with legacy routed session storage no longer land in an obsolete routed conversation by mistake. Valid scoped routed selections for the current gateway still survive reload, so real routed restores keep their intended behavior instead of being flattened.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Existing real-browser proof for this branch is preserved below under `## Real behavior proof`.\n- The current head `1869f9ea392766e5d0c083c666d80c3e9487dd73` merges `upstream/main` and carries the routed-session restore proof forward in the renamed Control UI settings/E2E layout.\n- Current-head validation after merging `upstream/main` onto `1869f9ea39`:\n  - `CI=true COREPACK_HOME=/home/node/.openclaw/workspace/agents/pr-machine/workspace/.corepack node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.ui.config.ts ui/src/ui/storage.node.test.ts ui/src/app/settings.node.test.ts --maxWorkers=1`\n  - `CI=true COREPACK_HOME=/home/node/.openclaw/workspace/agents/pr-machine/workspace/.corepack node scripts/run-tsgo.mjs -p test/tsconfig/tsconfig.test.ui.json --incremental false --pretty false`\n  - `CI=true COREPACK_HOME=/home/node/.openclaw/workspace/agents/pr-machine/workspace/.corepack node scripts/run-oxlint-shards.mjs`\n  - `git diff --check upstream/main...HEAD`\n  - `git merge-tree --write-tree HEAD upstream/main`\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n- Behavior or issue addressed: Control UI could reload into a stale historical routed session from older persisted top-level settings instead of reopening on the real `main` session, while valid scoped per-gateway routed selections still needed to survive reload.\n- Real environment tested: isolated temporary OpenClaw gateway plus a real Control UI browser session on `pi-pr-lab` / piclaw for branch proof commit `afa2413e82`; current head `2d718489a7da952b7188d3843e13d0e5a0ee5f2e` is a readability-only follow-up in the same restore helper and preserves the proved restore behavior.\n- Exact steps or command run after this patch:\n  1. Started an isolated temporary OpenClaw gateway for the PR branch.\n  2. Seeded Control UI storage with the historical routed direct/thread key `agent:main:telegram:direct:12345:thread:12345:99`.\n  3. Loaded the real Control UI in a browser and connected it to the temporary gateway.\n  4. Repeated the reload flow with a scoped `sessionsByGateway` routed key for the same gateway.\n  5. Revalidated current head `1869f9ea39` with `CI=true COREPACK_HOME=/home/node/.openclaw/workspace/agents/pr-machine/workspace/.corepack node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.ui.config.ts ui/src/ui/storage.node.test.ts ui/src/app/settings.node.test.ts --maxWorkers=1`, `CI=true COREPACK_HOME=/home/node/.openclaw/workspace/agents/pr-machine/workspace/.corepack node scripts/run-tsgo.mjs -p test/tsconfig/tsconfig.test.ui.json --incremental false --pretty false`, `CI=true COREPACK_HOME=/home/node/.openclaw/workspace/agents/pr-machine/workspace/.corepack node scripts/run-oxlint-shards.mjs`, `git diff --check upstream/main...HEAD`, and `git merge-tree --write-tree HEAD upstream/main`.\n- Evidence after fix: copied live browser proof already recorded on this PR shows `OpenClaw 2026.5.19 (f49955f)` running in an isolated temp gateway, successful RPCs `connect`, `sessions.subscribe`, `agents.list`, and `chat.history`, the UI restoring to `/chat?session=main`, the rendered page showing the main Chat session, and the historical routed key absent from the rendered DOM after restore. The same branch also carries browser-level Control UI E2E coverage in `ui/src/e2e/session-restore.e2e.test.ts` for both the legacy top-level reset path and the scoped per-gateway preservation path.\n- Observed result after fix: legacy top-level routed session values reopen on `main` instead of reviving a stale routed session, scoped per-gateway routed selections still restore for the active gateway, and the current exact head is back to maintainer-review state after the proof-capable review.\n- What was not tested: no separate fresh manual browser run was repeated after the `1869f9ea39` upstream refresh because this head preserves the same routed-session restore behavior while relocating the E2E proof test into upstream's new `ui/src/e2e/` layout and fixing the merged settings fallback bug; no live third-party production gateway/account was used.\n- Proof limitations or environment constraints: this worker container cannot launch local Chromium because `libglib-2.0.so.0` is missing, so the durable real-browser proof comes from the isolated `pi-pr-lab` run already attached to the PR history and the current head is validated locally with focused UI checks plus a clean merge-tree.\n- Before evidence: before this fix, current main and the latest release line could restore the stored top-level routed `sessionKey` unchanged, which reopened a stale routed session after reload instead of returning the UI to `main`.\n\n## Tests and validation\n\n- `CI=true COREPACK_HOME=/home/node/.openclaw/workspace/agents/pr-machine/workspace/.corepack node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.ui.config.ts ui/src/ui/storage.node.test.ts ui/src/app/settings.node.test.ts --maxWorkers=1`\n- `CI=true COREPACK_HOME=/home/node/.openclaw/workspace/agents/pr-machine/workspace/.corepack node scripts/run-tsgo.mjs -p test/tsconfig/tsconfig.test.ui.json --incremental false --pretty false`\n- `CI=true COREPACK_HOME=/home/node/.openclaw/workspace/agents/pr-machine/workspace/.corepack node scripts/run-oxlint-shards.mjs`\n- `git diff --check upstream/main...HEAD`\n- `git merge-tree --write-tree HEAD upstream/main`\n- Added browser-level Control UI reload coverage in `ui/src/e2e/session-restore.e2e.test.ts` for both the legacy top-level routed-key reset and scoped per-gateway routed-key preservation paths.\n- Expanded `ui/src/ui/storage.node.test.ts` coverage for valid and invalid historical routed restore shapes.\n\n## Risk checklist\n\n- User-visible behavior change: Yes.\n- Config, environment, or migration behavior change: Yes.\n- Security, auth, secrets, network, or tool execution behavior change: No.\n- Highest-risk area: compatibility-sensitive Control UI restore behavior for existing browser-local settings that still contain legacy top-level routed session keys.\n- Risk mitigation: the classifier change is confined to restore-time sanitization, valid scoped per-gateway routed selections are preserved explicitly, and both storage-level and browser-level regression coverage exercise the affected reload paths.\n\n## Current review state\n\nMerged current `upstream/main` into head `1869f9ea392766e5d0c083c666d80c3e9487dd73`, resolved the Control UI settings rename plus routed-session E2E path move inside PR scope, and revalidated the refreshed head with focused UI Vitest, UI TS compile, direct oxlint shards, `git diff --check`, and a clean `git merge-tree --write-tree HEAD upstream/main`. Requesting fresh ClawSweeper review on this new head.",
